From: mtbl23 <mtbl23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:23:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Leaf port: read the noise biome of a loaded chunk directly

Level#getNoiseBiome (used by BiomeManager for every biome, environment
attribute and mob spawn lookup) went through the generic chunk lookup with
status BIOMES: chunk holder map lookup, getChunkIfPresent, and the
ImposterProtoChunk wrapper that only delegates to the full chunk. If the full
chunk is loaded it is now read straight from the full chunk map; every other
case takes the old path.

Behaviour: identical (the wrapper delegates to the same LevelChunk).

Motivated by Leaf's chunk lookup patches ("optimize get chunk", "Optimize
LevelChunk#getBlockStateFinal"); independent implementation.
Leaf: https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/Level.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/Level.java
index ab49bb83b51a3ac210f4c51ec48c11036912149e..2af453244f4e0a1cf0a56b7e41de28b7276bf04e 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/Level.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/Level.java
@@ -816,6 +816,12 @@ public abstract class Level implements LevelAccessor, AutoCloseable, ca.spottedl
      */
     @Override
     public Holder<Biome> getNoiseBiome(final int x, final int y, final int z) {
+        // Leaf port start - a loaded full chunk is looked up directly instead of through the chunk holder (same data, the status BIOMES wrapper just delegates to it)
+        final LevelChunk fullChunk = ((ServerLevel)this).getChunkSource().getChunkAtIfLoadedImmediately(x >> 2, z >> 2);
+        if (fullChunk != null) {
+            return fullChunk.getNoiseBiome(x, y, z);
+        }
+        // Leaf port end
         final ChunkAccess chunk = this.getChunk(x >> 2, z >> 2, ChunkStatus.BIOMES, false);
 
         return chunk != null ? chunk.getNoiseBiome(x, y, z) : this.getUncachedNoiseBiome(x, y, z);
